  <CATEGORY Name="Ending">
  	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_0">GODDAMMIT NEIL[br][br]We can't just scrap the whole plot at the last minute because you "don't like it" or think ChatGPT could do better. The only reason I'm here in the first place is because you ran out of AI tokens, and needed a REAL writer to fix your complete mess of a project. So I draft up a whole fancy new story, and what do you do? You THROW IT AWAY!!![br][br]DEAR PLAYER: Attached is my full, 124 page story pitch for Bunker's Edge. I didn't have time to port over all the fancy ImGUI stuff from SOMA, so just use Debug Action #3 to advance to the next page. Very important.</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_1">ROUTE A: BUNKER'S EDGE[br][br]- Henri(tm) falls into the Portal of Charon and wakes up in a futuristic, copyright-free parkour level[br][br]- The player picks up collectable notes throughout the level that hint at Henri(tm) being in a timeloop[br][br]- The player completes the level, sees a stat screen, and warps to The Hallway of Realities. The Hallway has various Experiment rooms such as the Dying Room, Date Room, Time Room, Snail Room, Standing Room, etc.[br][br]- The player enters the Dying Room and dies by quantum suicide.</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_2">ROUTE B: THE BEAST(tm)[br][br]- The player is forced to play the game again, this time as the Beast(tm) [can we just reuse the stock player moveset and add a super jump?][br][br]- The Beast(tm) is aware of the time loop and is desperately trying to stop Henri(tm) from reaching The Hallway Of Realities. His various monster noises are translated into speech during this route (ex: "Henri(tm), no! Don't go to The Hallway!").[br][br]- The Beast(tm) is forced to watch as Henri(tm) warps to The Hallway of Realities, where he will inevitably die.</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_3">ROUTE C: ENDING[br][br]- The player replays the game as normal but with glitchy textures/objects phasing in and out of existence [TODO: Throw in a bunch of random assets from popular games]. The players warps to The Hallway as normal.[br][br]- The Beast(tm) follows Henri(tm) to The Hallway(tm), and reveals that both he and Henri(tm) are mental constructs created by a dying WWI veteran(tm), to better cope with their "trauma" and imminent death.[br][br]- Henri(tm) accepts this, reenforcing the theme with a moving speech, before he dissolves into nothingness and we roll credits.</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_4">What do you think, dear player?[br][br]Surely this is a better story than whatever the hell Neil's planning for the release version. A 1:1 ripoff of Mirror's Edge with no other context is not going to win us *anything* except for a lawsuit. Which we will lose. Please don't let us get sued.[br][br]- Maurice</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_5">CUT CONTENT NOTES[br][br]These are some of the cut notes from MY version of the story.[br]Also I binded this terminal to the exact same debug action as the other one since all the other debug actions were full, so good luck reading them both at once!</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_6">CUT CONTENT NOTE #12:[br][br]What is reality? This is a question that I ask myself every day. One minute I am trapped in a bunker with horrors beyond comprehension, and the next I am jumping around like a madman in a city of glass![br][br]I have been to many places, and many times, but this is the most unique. It lies at the outer edge of existence, somewhere between reality and fantasy. Reason and chaos. I hope to one day understand its mysteries.[br][br]-Henri(tm)</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_7">CUT CONTENT #16:[br][br]I have long wondered why this place is called the The Hallway of Realities. It is a hallway, no doubt, but it looks like only one reality to me![br][br]Lambert would be laughing at me now. It is a wordplay, a trick. This is the hallway of *realities*: Things that are real. The expression of abstract concepts in literal form. I'm not yet certain what all the rooms represent, but I am excited to learn![br][br]- Henri(tm)</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_8">CUT CONTENT #22:[br][br]The manifestation of the Sitting Room frightens me. Unlike the others, it represents nothing but cold, infinite darkness. It is the world between worlds, the space between spaces. What is not eating away at what is.[br][br]I fear I must brave the Dead Room. My life will be decided by a simple coin toss, it seems. May fate be at my side, and if she falters...[br][br]May my creator welcome me with open arms.[br][br]- Henri(tm)</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_9">What do you think, dear player?[br][br]Isn't this all so very fun? Playing meta with you? I can make up any story I want, and you'll believe me! And even if you don't, you can't prove that this isn't reality. All you know for sure is what's right in front of your eyes. And even then! Kihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihi!</Entry>
  </CATEGORY>
